// Curated self-naming pool for a Blade boon's conjured weapon, banded by the
// wielder's Ethos.moral() at the moment tier 5 ("Nombrada") unlocks -- see
// common/src/comp/pact.rs's `blade_names_manifest` and `Pact::blade_name`.
// Never player-authored text: every entry here is pre-approved content, so
// no profanity/length filter is needed at the call site.
//
// Tone: per docs/design/lore/chargen/classes/warlock.md's "Pact of the
// Blade" entry, the un-awakened weapon is described as having "no opinions,
// no hunger, and no name to keep secret" -- a nameless tool. Tier 5 is that
// tool crossing into sentience and choosing what it is. Names below lean on
// oath/debt/covenant vocabulary shared across all three bands, differing in
// how that vocabulary reads: Good = a vow kept, Neutral = a bargain whose
// terms nobody else can read, Evil = a debt collected in full.
{
    Good: [
        "Dawnoath",
        "Gracehallow",
        "Sworn Mercy",
        "Vow-Bright",
        "Lucent Absolution",
    ],
    Neutral: [
        "Quietus",
        "Hollowmark",
        "The Unspoken Edge",
        "Between-Tide",
        "Fardebt",
    ],
    Evil: [
        "Gravethirst",
        "Sinmaw",
        "The Last Confession",
        "Bloodcovenant",
        "Wraithfang",
    ],
}
